    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter the July 5th slate with a focus on exploiting high-leverage spots against shaky arms. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Andy Pages** (71.11) headline the lineup as our most potent options, both benefiting significantly from the soft matchup against Chandler and JP Sears, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** (70.61) remains an elite start despite a challenging matchup against Lodolo; his ability to overcome negative platoon splits through raw talent and a prime lead-off spot keeps his efficiency score firmly in the \"Strong\" territory. Furthermore, **Heliot Ramos** is an intriguing play at 59.50; while he faces Gordon, the combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and a slow opposing delivery provides a sneaky stolen base upside that justifies the aggressive start.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Nolan Schanuel** (49.79), who narrowly missed the cut. While **Nolan Schanuel** projects as a stable contributor, the optimizer leaned into the higher ceiling provided by **Dominic Smith** (43.33) and the categorical depth of our primary core. We are keeping a close eye on the bench, as **Josh Lowe** (41.62) possesses elite sprint speed that we value highly in our 5x5 format; however, his struggle against the handedness of Ranger Suarez kept him on the pine. As we look at the slate, caution is advised with **Jackson Merrill**, whose projection is currently tethered to an assumed #7 spot in the order; should he move lower, his efficiency could dip further. **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks** also face high-skill arms in McLean and Jump, necessitating a disciplined approach to our daily game caps if these catchers fail to capitalize on their limited opportunities early in the series.",
